SUMMARY:Deadline: A4 Residency Art Center: International Residency Fellowsh
 ip 2028 (Chengdu)
DESCRIPTION:The A4 Residency Art Center in Chengdu\, the residency platform
  of the A4 Art Museum in Luxelakes Eco-City\, opens its full-year 2028 rec
 ruitment.\n\nOrganisation: A4 Residency Art Center (A4 Art Museum)\nLocati
 on: Luxelakes Eco-City\, Tianfu New Area\, Chengdu\, China. Open worldwide
 .\nAward: Fully funded fellowship: private studio and accommodation\, roun
 d-trip economy airfare or second-class train ticket within a set budget\, 
 and a production grant of RMB 10\,000 per person/team for materials and pr
 oduction (excluding living expenses). No application fee.\nDuration: Appro
 ximately 8 weeks\, in the Spring 2028 (April to June) or Autumn 2028 (July
  to October) cycle.\n\nMore: https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residencyar
 tcenter/residing/latest-recruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residencyartcenter/residing/latest-re
 cruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Luxelakes Eco-City\, Tianfu New Area\, Chengdu\, China. Open world
 wide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:yao-residency-02-taiwan-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261111T002446Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: YAO Residency #02 (Taiwan): Research Residency 2027 and E
 xhibition 2028
DESCRIPTION:YAO Residency #02 centres on the translation between culture an
 d material: through living\, research and exchange in Taiwan\, artists eng
 age with different cultural contexts\, local ways of living\, materials an
 d craft practices\, with emphasis on process rather than finished works. O
 NE artist/practitioner is selected for a two-phase program.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: YAO Residency Program (Yao Zuo Zhu Cun Ji Hua)\nLocation: Taiwan. Open 
 worldwide to applicants aged 18 and above\, regardless of nationality\; in
 ternational artists arrange their own entry and visa (YAO can provide an i
 nvitation letter).\nAward: Research Residency 2027: travel support (intern
 ational applicants reimbursed up to NTD 20\,000 for one round-trip to Taiw
 an against receipts)\, production budget up to NTD 20\,000\, living stipen
 d of NTD 10\,000\, accommodation\, Open Studio venue\, local connections\,
  and documentation\, text editing\, translation and promotional support. E
 xhibition Phase 2028: travel support up to NTD 20\,000 again\, a further N
 TD 10\,000 living stipend\, accommodation\, exhibition venue at YAO\, inst
 allation and de-installation assistance\, and exhibition documentation. Ap
 plication fee: NTD 300 for Taiwan-based applicants (bank transfer) or USD 
 10 for international applicants (PayPal)\, non-refundable.\nDuration: Two 
 phases: research residency 21 August to 21 November 2027 with Open Studio 
 27 October to 16 November 2027\, then a formal exhibition at YAO in 2028 (
 expected to run at least six weeks\, dates agreed with the artist). The se
 lected artist commits to both phases.\n\nMore: https://docs.google.com/for
 ms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfQ5-RBrfPckf4O9A5LeDrAzbFlXHzBkYrpPyTiy3HeKc8BkQ/viewform?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfQ5-RBrfPckf4O9A5LeDrAzbFlXHz
 BkYrpPyTiy3HeKc8BkQ/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Taiwan. Open worldwide to applicants aged 18 and above\, regardles
 s of nationality\; international artists arrange their own entry and visa 
 (YAO can provide an invitation letter).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:daiwa-foundation-small-grants-march-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261111T002446Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270331
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270401
SUMMARY:Deadline: Daiwa Foundation Small Grants\, March 2027 round (GBP 2\,
 000-9\,000 for UK-Japan projects)
DESCRIPTION:The Daiwa Foundation Small Grants support projects that promote
  interaction between the UK and Japan in any field\, including arts exchan
 ges\, exhibitions\, conferences\, grassroots and educational exchanges and
  research travel\, with travel between the two countries as the main focus
 .\n\nOrganisation: Daiwa Anglo-Japanese Foundation\nLocation: For individu
 als\, societies\, associations and other bodies in the UK or Japan running
  projects that connect the two countries.\nAward: GBP 2\,000 to 9\,000 (ty
 pical awards GBP 3\,000-4\,000)\; flights up to GBP 1\,200 each and subsis
 tence up to GBP 100 per person per day. A contribution\, not full funding.
  No application fee.\nDuration: Per project\; activity can start from late
  May or early June 2027.\n\nMore: https://dajf.org.uk/grants-awards-and-pr
 izes/daiwa-foundation-small-grants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://dajf.org.uk/grants-awards-and-prizes/daiwa-foundation-small-gra
 nts?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:For individuals\, societies\, associations and other bodies in the
  UK or Japan running projects that connect the two countries.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
